    "updated_at": "2024-06-24T13:54:44Z",
    "body": "The solution you present that exists today is different to the mechanics of `CloseWatcher`'s `signal` property. It seems like you're suggesting the `signal` should call `hidePopover` after a certain time, is this correct?\r\n\r\nCan you explain the broader motivating use case for this please? Are you trying to make time sensitive UI? Time based UI is not in conformance with [WCAG 2.2.3](https://www.w3.org/WAI/WCAG22/Techniques/general/G5.html) and so ideally we would not encode such patterns into the web.",
